{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-01T21:06:24.582Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"b343c237d9dd86b74913bb91","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-1rfy0y","claim:pm-btv6x7","claim:pm-gh1631","claim:pm-wftvem","claim:pm-y4v90c","lineage:pm-gh1631","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-1rfy0y+pm-btv6x7+pm-gh1631+pm-wftvem+pm-y4v90c","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-1rfy0y","claim:pm-btv6x7","claim:pm-gh1631","claim:pm-wftvem","claim:pm-y4v90c","lineage:pm-gh1631","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.316","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-01T21:06:24.582Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-01T21:06:24.581Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Root cause: buildInvalidArgumentGuidance classified any message containing \" must be \" or \" requires \" as invalid_argument_value, and applyPmCliErrorContext only replaced the generic title for command_failed. The likely_duplicate refusal interpolates candidate item titles into its message, so a duplicate whose title contains either phrase was classified as a bad flag value. It got the \"Invalid argument value\" headline and the misleading \"Check allowed values in command help\" next step.\n\nFix (src/cli/error-guidance.ts): substring heuristics now classify only untyped text. A typed code keeps the invalid-argument route only when its message starts with \"Invalid \" or it declares an allowed domain. Whenever a typed code overrides a generic class (command_failed or invalid_argument_value), the headline is the message's first line. JSON title and code agree, and generic-coded refusals keep the class title.\n\nNegative control: the published 2026.11.1 tarball's dist/cli/error-guidance.js returns title \"Invalid argument value\" plus the \"Check allowed values\" step for the same input. The new case in tests/unit/cli/error-guidance.spec.ts asserts the typed first-line headline in JSON, in classification and on the first line of the human output.\n"}]}],"before_hash":"c3f71995bf5dee927c92d3d9026489f12d0f296a889e1212691125c7a1f44b0c","after_hash":"1643c2f65c1824f3b90c30c18132929dfbda62b20bda142a9ab0a3731326b86b","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"af8895183ad38d2b47f664261d21a01041f4ba566ac25916c3f5eeecc47c0155"}
